# Are there many people growing their own vegetables now?
Yes, I think more people are growing their own vegetables nowadays, especially after the COVID-19 pandemic. Many people have become more concerned about food safety and the quality of the produce they consume, so they prefer growing vegetables themselves whenever possible.

Another reason is that gardening can be a relaxing and rewarding hobby. People enjoy watching plants grow and harvesting fresh vegetables that they have grown with their own effort. It also helps reduce grocery expenses to some extent.

Of course, not everyone has enough space or time to maintain a vegetable garden, particularly those living in apartments or busy urban areas. However, with the growing interest in healthy lifestyles and sustainable living, I believe home gardening has become increasingly popular in recent years.

# Do you think it’s good to let kids learn how to plant?
Yes, definitely. I think it's a good idea to teach children how to plant and take care of plants from a young age.

First of all, gardening helps children develop important qualities such as patience, responsibility, and perseverance because plants need regular care and take time to grow. It also teaches them that good results often come from consistent effort.

Another benefit is that it helps children understand where food comes from and encourages them to appreciate nature more. Nowadays, many children grow up in urban areas and spend a lot of time indoors, so gardening can be a great opportunity for them to connect with the natural world.

Besides that, planting can be a fun and rewarding activity. Children often feel excited when they see a seed grow into a plant, which can spark their curiosity and interest in science and the environment.

Overall, I think gardening is both educational and enjoyable, so it's definitely a valuable activity for children.

# What do you think of the job of a farmer?
I think farming is one of the most important professions in society because farmers are responsible for producing the food that we eat every day.

However, it's also a very demanding job. Farmers often have to work long hours and deal with challenges such as unpredictable weather, crop diseases, and fluctuating market prices. Sometimes, despite putting in a lot of effort, they may not earn a stable income because many factors are beyond their control.

In addition, modern farming requires more than just physical labor. Farmers need knowledge of agriculture, technology, and even basic business management to run their farms effectively.

Overall, I have a lot of respect for farmers because their work is essential to both society and the economy, yet they often don't receive the recognition they deserve.

# What are the differences between traditional and modern agriculture?
I think the biggest difference is the way farming is carried out. Traditional agriculture mainly relies on manual labor and simple tools, whereas modern agriculture makes extensive use of machinery and technology.

For example, in the past, farmers often planted and harvested crops by hand. Nowadays, many farms use tractors, automated irrigation systems, and even drones to monitor crops. As a result, farming has become much more efficient and productive.

However, traditional farming is often considered more environmentally friendly because it uses fewer chemicals and focuses more on natural farming methods. In contrast, modern agriculture can increase food production, but it may also create environmental challenges if not managed properly.

Overall, both approaches have their own advantages and disadvantages.
